    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d266">

                <pb facs="0276" n="268" xml:id="pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9435: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-19T17:00:00-04:00">August 19, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>162. Your 448 of August 16, 3 p.m., and Tokyo’s 278 of August 18, 5 p.m.<anchor
                        n="61" xml:id="d266-f1"/> In view of large number of Americans at Kuling and
                    of Japanese Navy Department’s instruction to Japanese naval forces to refrain
                    from bombing Kuling unless it is used as a base for Chinese military operations,
                    please ask Chinese authorities to refrain from military operations which would
                    be likely to bring hostilities into the neighborhood of Kuling.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d266-f1" n="61" xml:id="d266-f1-content">
